## Built in the open

::: {.bms-section-lead}
The website and most of the tools behind it are open source. You can inspect the code, check the methods, report a problem, or reuse parts of the work.
:::

::: {.bms-inline-note}
Backgammon engines are useful, but they are not magic. When the method matters, we show the assumptions, limitations, source code, and supporting data behind the result.

Some projects also use public data from external services such as OpenGammon. Public data does not necessarily mean that the service itself is open source.
:::

